From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Haseenesss <Haseenesss@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 10:00:18 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] build_ipa_from_nsp: reuse the other platform's RomFS image
 (--romfs-from)

A Mac app and an iPhone build of the same game read the same RomFS.img, but a build
whose build folder is gone extracted it again, though the other build had left a copy
(the Mac app's Contents/Resources/romfs.img, the launcher's games/<title ID>/romfs.img).

A fresh extraction now writes RomFS.img.id beside the image: the title, program, version
and --allow-damaged it was read with, the content IDs of the base and update packages'
NCAs (the first 16 bytes of each NCA's SHA-256), the image's size and SHA-256.
pack_app.py copies it into the app as Resources/romfs.img.id. --romfs-from IMAGE
(repeatable) names such images: one is taken in place of extracting the RomFS when its
identity file names this title, version and these packages' content IDs, its bytes hash
to the recorded SHA-256, the index is whole, and its files (path, size, first 32 bytes)
are the ones the packages hold, which nx_extract --manifest lists without writing the
RomFS. Anything else is extracted as before. An older extraction reused without an
identity gets none: it was never checked against the packages.

LNPANDY/NX2Apple#708

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#1623 (upstream without the nxb build hook)
Reason: the launcher reuses the other platform's romfs.img until upstream merges --romfs-from
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#708
